{
 "graph": {
  "name": "corne-cherry-left",
  "version": "1.0",
  "date": "2026-10-31",
  "description": "The Corne keyboard v4 (foostan/crkbd, corne-cherry hotswap), left half as published: USB-C with 5.1 kΩ CC resistors and ESD protection, a Schottky to +5V, an NCP1117LP 3.3 V regulator, an RP2040 with 16 MB QSPI flash and a 12 MHz crystal, 21 keys and 2 extra keys in hot-swap sockets each on its own GPIO (no matrix), 23 SK6812MINI-E RGB LEDs in one chain one diode below +5V, a TRS jack to the right half, an OLED header, BOOT and RESET buttons. Transcribed for edakit's tests.",
  "purpose": {
   "use": "private",
   "market": "EU",
   "notes": "An open keyboard that makers order and build for themselves; vendors also sell kits. The transcription is a test of edakit, not a product."
  },
  "conventions": {
   "pin_reference": "'<designator>.<pin>' with the pin numbers of the Corne's KiCad symbols (= its footprints' pads); the encoder positions EXSW1/2 with the socket's pins 1 (S1) and 2 (S2)",
